# Autopilot Runtime vs Claude Code Substrate Gap Audit

Generated: 2026-05-27

## Verdict

Autopilot is green against the current default harness and Antigravity parity-plus claims, but it is not yet parity-plus against the broader `examples/claude-code-main` substrate.

The Claude Code example is a terminal-first, CLI/SDK-native substrate with a wide tool registry, streaming tool execution, rich permission rule grammar, hook lifecycle, deferred tool discovery, task/team surfaces, skills/plugins/slash commands, and context-analysis/compaction machinery. Autopilot is stronger in IDE/product-facing run proof, daemon-owned governance, managed browser/computer session UX, tracing separation, coding receipts, and Antigravity-style workbench parity. Those are different centers of gravity.

This audit is source-and-evidence based. I did not run a fresh live GUI proof campaign for Claude Code-specific rows.

