## Decisive Read

Do not treat Claude Code parity as a repeat of the Rust catalogue campaign. The catalogue and Antigravity work already proved our default IDE harness lane. A Claude Code parity-plus campaign should target the substrate pieces that would actually improve Autopilot:

1. Streaming tool executor semantics: tool calls while stream blocks arrive, safe parallelism, exclusive tool serialization, sibling cancellation.
2. Rich permission grammar: rule source/destination model, accept-edits/plan/dont-ask/bypass equivalents, classifier-backed auto-review, bridge callbacks.
3. Context analyzer and compaction dashboard: token categories, tool-result budgets, deferred tool/MCP accounting, compact/restore semantics.
4. Hook lifecycle: pre/post/denied/stop/task/session/compact hooks with blocking continuation rules.
5. Deferred tools and MCP: model-visible tool search, MCP auth/resources/prompts/skills, server approval, and dynamic context loading.
6. Task/team substrate: task lists, background tasks, peer messaging, team lanes, and retained output files.
7. Skills/plugins/slash command runtime: if Autopilot wants Claude-style extensibility, wire it as product runtime, not only operator-side Codex skills.
8. CLI/SDK/headless bridge: only if Autopilot wants to compete as a terminal SDK substrate in addition to IDE Agent Studio.

## Product Recommendation

Autopilot should not clone Claude Code blindly. Keep the IDE-first daemon-owned harness as the product spine, then selectively import the high-leverage Claude substrate ideas:

- P0: streaming tool executor, permission grammar, hook lifecycle, context analyzer, deferred MCP/tool search.
- P1: task/team substrate, shell background/stall ergonomics, runtime skills/plugins.
- P2: CLI/SDK/headless parity and long-tail tools, unless product strategy explicitly expands into terminal-first workflows.

The next campaign should be named as a Claude Code substrate parity-plus campaign, with live IDE proof only for UX-impacting surfaces and static/SDK proof accepted for CLI-only rows.
